Subject: [PATCH 32/43] Metal diamond engine: reciprocals from the host; fused
 Mur Post and Apply beside sheets (snapshot cg30e)

The divisions by run-time widths (the cell loop, the z faces of Mur, the UPML loop) use the high word of a product
with ceil(2^32 / w): a table for the tile widths 2..64 in the kernel source and a field of the UPML record, guarded
so that the quotient is exact. They are not computed on the GPU: on an M5 (macOS 27.0.1) its 0xffffffff / w returns
3579139454 for w = 3 (1431655765 is right), which diamond_check.sh caught as wrong fields in a build that did.
Post and Apply of the Mur faces of one axis are also done in one go in tiles with sheets or lumped elements when the
Mur faces come first in the Apply order. diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical.

